Question: Which finding is in this chest X-ray?
Options: {"A": "left upper lobe pulmonary atelectasis", "B": "right upper lobe pulmonary atelectasis"}

Execution:
1. [task] Which finding is in this chest X-ray?
Options: {"A": "left upper lobe pulmonary atelectasis", "B": "right upper lobe pulmonary atelectasis"}
2. [action] {"calls":[{"tool":"chest_xray_expert","args":{"question":"Describe any signs of pulmonary atelectasis in this lateral chest X-ray, specifically noting the location (upper vs lower) and any evidence suggesting left or right side involvement."}}],"reason":"Need expert analysis to identify atelectasis location and laterality on this lateral view"}
3. [action] {"calls":[{"tool":"llava_med_qa","args":{"question":"Does this lateral chest X-ray show upper lobe atelectasis? If so, is it more consistent with left or right upper lobe based on the location of opacity and fissure displacement?"}}],"reason":"Obtain independent second opinion on upper lobe atelectasis laterality since first tool suggested lower lobe which conflicts with options"}
4. [action] {"calls":[{"tool":"medgemma","args":{"question":"On this lateral chest X-ray, is there evidence of upper lobe atelectasis? If present, describe the location and any features that help distinguish left from right upper lobe involvement."}}],"reason":"Seek third independent opinion to resolve conflict between tools regarding atelectasis location and laterality"}
5. [action] {"calls":[{"tool":"llava_rad","args":{"question":"Does this lateral chest X-ray demonstrate right upper lobe atelectasis? Describe the opacity location and fissure displacement to support your answer."}}],"reason":"Obtain a fourth independent expert opinion specifically focused on confirming right upper lobe atelectasis features"}
6. [action] {"calls":[{"tool":"medvlm_r1","args":{"question":"On this lateral chest X-ray, is there evidence of upper lobe atelectasis? If so, does the location and appearance favor right or left upper lobe involvement?"}}],"reason":"Obtain fifth independent opinion to resolve conflicting tool outputs regarding atelectasis laterality"}
7. [action] {"calls":[{"tool":"verify","args":{"proposed_answer":"B. right upper lobe pulmonary atelectasis","risk":"Conflicting tool outputs: chest_xray_expert said RLL, llava_med_qa and medgemma said RUL, llava_rad said normal/clear, medvlm_r1 failed. Need to confirm if RUL atelectasis is truly present on this lateral view given the disagreement."}}],"reason":"Audit conflicting evidence before finalizing answer due to significant disagreement among tools"}
8. [action] {"answer":"B. right upper lobe pulmonary atelectasis","reason":"Verifier confirmed correctness of RUL atelectasis despite lateral view limitations and conflicting tool outputs."}
9. [released_benchmark_feedback] Historical reference: B. right upper lobe pulmonary atelectasis

